{
  "Tabs show one panel at a time under a strip of tabs: from JSX or programmatically, closable, with icons and badges, scroll buttons when the tabs do not fit, four placements and panels built when they are first shown.": "",
  "A `<Tab>`'s children are its panel. `value` is the selected tab's `key` (else its index) and `x-model` binds it two-way. Created with `new`, tabs are added, inserted and removed programmatically.": "",
  "Closable tabs": "",
  "A close button on every tab (`closable`), or on some (a tab's own `closable` wins). Delete or a middle click closes the focused or pointed tab. `onClose` can cancel: ask about unsaved work first.": "",
  "Many tabs": "",
  "When the tabs do not fit, arrow buttons scroll the strip (`scrollButtons`, on by default); the selected tab and the one with focus scroll into view.": "",
  "Manual activation": "",
  "By default an arrow key selects the tab it moves to. With `activation=\"manual\"` it only moves focus and Enter or Space selects: better when a panel is slow to show.": "",
  "Icons, badges, disabled tabs": "",
  "Lazy panels": "",
  "A panel is built the first time it is shown and kept afterwards, so what was typed in it stays (`lazy`, on by default; `lazy={false}` builds every panel at once). A tab with a `content` factory and `keepAlive={false}` has its content disposed while hidden and made again when it shows. JSX children are made once by the page, so they are always kept.": "",
  "Into the strip, onto the selected tab; again, into its panel.": "",
  "The previous / next tab, wrapping around (reversed in right-to-left text). With `start` and `end` placement: Up / Down.": "",
  "The first / last tab.": "",
  "Select the focused tab (with `activation=\"manual\"`).": "",
  "Closes the focused tab when it is closable.": "",
  "Selects that tab and focuses it (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "`tablist`, `tab` (a `<button>`) and `tabpanel`; `aria-orientation=\"vertical\"` with `start` and `end` placement.": "",
  "`aria-selected` on the tabs; `aria-controls` ties a tab to its panel and `aria-labelledby` names the panel by its tab.": "",
  "One Tab stop in the strip (the selected tab). A panel with nothing focusable in it takes focus itself (`tabindex=\"0\"`), so its text can be reached.": "",
  "`aria-disabled=\"true\"`; the arrow keys skip them.": "",
  "Not a Tab stop and hidden from screen readers (a button inside a tab would be a control inside a control); Delete closes the tab and `aria-keyshortcuts=\"Delete\"` announces it. Its tooltip comes from `uiLocale`.": "",
  "For the pointer only, hidden from screen readers: the arrow keys reach every tab and scroll it into view.": "",
  "Tabs write one text: the close button's tooltip, `uiLocale.strings.close`. Every tab follows a change at once.": "",
  "The root. `data-placement`, `data-variant`, `data-size`, `data-stretch`, `data-overflow`, `data-scroll-buttons`, `data-disabled`.": "",
  "The strip and the tab list in it (the scroll box).": "",
  "A tab: `aria-selected`, `aria-disabled`, `data-closable`.": "",
  "The parts of a tab.": "",
  "A scroll button: `data-direction` (`back`, `forward`), `data-end` when it has nowhere to go.": "",
  "The panels and a panel (the tab's own element).": "",
  "Units: the whole, the strip with its line along the panel (`bottom`, `start`, `end`; the pill tray: `pill`, `pill-bottom` …), the row of tabs, the scroll buttons and their glyph.": "",
  "Units: a tab in each state (`hover`, `pressed`, `selected`, `disabled`, `focus`; in the pill variant `pill`, `pill-hover` …) and its parts.": "",
  "Units: the line variant's mark (`vertical`, `hover`, `selected`, `selected-disabled`), a line between two tabs, the panel (`pill`, `pill-across`, `focus`).": "",
  "Sizes per size class.": "",
  "Where the layout puts the pieces: between pills, over the strip's line, the mark, the close button, a vertical strip's width.": "",
  "Outward curves at the selected tab's corners on the panel's side, in its fill.": "",
  "Tabs props": "",
  "the first tab": "",
  "The selected tab's `key`, else its index. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "The selected tab's index in `tabs`.": "",
  "Names the tab list for screen readers (`aria-label`). The same property as `text`.": "",
  "`auto`: an arrow key selects the tab it moves to. `manual`: arrows move focus only; Enter or Space selects.": "",
  "`top`, `bottom`, `start`, `end`. `start` and `end` stack the tabs vertically.": "",
  "`line`: a bar on the selected tab. `pill`: the tabs sit on a tray and the selected one is raised.": "",
  "The tabs share the whole width.": "",
  "Arrow buttons at the ends of the strip when the tabs do not fit. Off: a thin scroll bar.": "",
  "Every tab gets a close button. A tab's own `closable` wins.": "",
  "A panel is built when it is first shown, then kept. A tab's own `lazy` wins.": "",
  "`false`: what a tab's `content` made is disposed while the tab is hidden and made again when it shows. A tab's own `keepAlive` wins.": "",
  "The shared properties of every control. `tabStop={false}` takes the tab strip out of the Tab order.": "",
  "Tab props": "",
  "The caption; `&General` makes Alt+G select the tab. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "Names the tab in `value`. The JSX `key` works too.": "",
  "A short text after the title (a count); empty or `null` shows none.": "",
  "the Tabs": "",
  "A close button on this tab.": "",
  "This tab's own setting.": "",
  "Makes the panel content when the panel is built: instead of, or after, the JSX children.": "",
  "`false`: the tab cannot be selected and the arrow keys skip it.": "",
  "`false`: the tab is left out; a selected one hands the selection to a neighbour.": "",
  "The tabs, in strip order.": "",
  "The selected `Tab`, `null` when there is none.": "",
  "Whether the tab is selected; whether it shows a close button.": "",
  "Whether its panel has been built.": "",
  "Its `Tabs`; its button in the strip. A tab's own element is its panel.": "",
  "Adds a tab at the end. A tab of another `Tabs` moves here.": "",
  "Adds a tab at an index.": "",
  "Removes the tab and disposes it; no `onClose`. The selection and focus move to a neighbour.": "",
  "Selects a tab programmatically; `false` when it is hidden or not there.": "",
  "Closes a tab as its close button does: `onClose` can cancel it.": "",
  "Focuses the selected tab.": "",
  "The same, from the tab.": "",
  "The user is about to select a tab. `e`: `{ tab, index, previousTab, previousIndex, cancel, source, event }`; `e.cancel = true` keeps the current one.": "",
  "The selected tab changed. `e`: `{ tab, index, previousTab, previousIndex, byUser, source, event? }`.": "",
  "A tab is about to close, by its button, Delete, a middle click or `close()`. `e`: `{ tab, index, byUser, cancel, source, event? }`.": ""
